{
 "version": 1,
 "about": "The bike's materials (since the 2026-10-31a build; one per shape, the needle's too since its blade glows). harley_meshes.py reads each material's labels and shader keys (shader, cube, env_scale, smoothness, spec_colour, spec_mult, emit, alpha, two_sided, cast_shadows_worn, cast_shadows_parked) into the nifs' shader blocks; bike_textures.py reads the rest: texture sizes, which surface each piece material (and glTF mesh, surface_overrides) gets, the surfaces' looks (surface_types: colours sRGB hex, spec = _s red, smooth = _s green, both 0..1) and the art files of the fixed-UV labels, and writes Textures/CMB/Bike/<mat>_{d,n,s[,g]}.dds and Materials/CMB/Bike/<mat>.bgsm (parked; none for the lit overlays the parked nif leaves out) and <mat>_worn.bgsm. Cubes: CH MetalChrome01Cube_e, DI mipblur_DefaultOutside1_dielectric, GL shinyglass_e (vanilla), MR our mirror_cube_e.",
